# expected.querier.log
# attestation: spec-derived from IEEE 1516.1-2010 references below
# Cross-check status: not yet cross-checked (2-federate scenario; reproducible via the external commercial-RTI harness against any DLC-conformant RTI)
# canonicalization: cppsdk/tests/dlc/conformance/_harness/normalize.py
# spec-cites: see README.md
# Per IEEE 1516.1-2010 §4.2, §4.9, §6.9, §7.17, §7.18, §4.10:
# GOLDEN AMENDED (M37, 2026-07-02, specification review):
#   Original golden expected `ATTRIBUTE_IS_OWNED_BY_RTI
#   attr=HLAprivilegeToDelete`. That is wrong for this scenario: the
#   carrier — a joined federate — registers car-query, and §6.8
#   (registerObjectInstance) makes the REGISTRANT the owner of the
#   instance attribute HLAprivilegeToDeleteObject. §7.18
#   attributeIsOwnedByRTI applies only to RTI-owned instance
#   attributes (MOM-managed instances per §6.8/§10; not
#   federate-registered ones). Correct §7.18 answer is therefore
#   informAttributeOwnership with the carrier as owner. See README
#   "Golden review" for the full adjudication.
# Two of three §7.18 callback flavors exercised in a single run
# (informAttributeOwnership ×2, attributeIsNotOwned ×1); a true
# attributeIsOwnedByRTI witness needs an RTI-owned (MOM) instance
# attribute, out of scope for this fixture.
# RO-bucket: the three INFORM/IS_NOT_OWNED/IS_OWNED_BY_RTI callback
# orderings depend on RTI scheduling; harness LBTS-bucket sort
# normalizes against this.
QUERIER: CONNECT
QUERIER: JOIN
QUERIER: DISCOVER name=car-query handle=<H>
QUERIER: QUERY_OWNERSHIP attr=OwnedAttr
QUERIER: QUERY_OWNERSHIP attr=UnownedAttr
QUERIER: QUERY_OWNERSHIP attr=HLAprivilegeToDelete
QUERIER: INFORM_OWNERSHIP attr=OwnedAttr owner=<H>
QUERIER: ATTRIBUTE_IS_NOT_OWNED attr=UnownedAttr
QUERIER: INFORM_OWNERSHIP attr=HLAprivilegeToDelete owner=<H>  # §6.8: registrant owns HLAprivilegeToDeleteObject
QUERIER: RESIGN
